In this project, I implemented a Switch Case program using C++.
* Accepted user input to select a day number.
* Used the switch-case statement to handle multiple conditions efficiently.
* Mapped numerical values to corresponding day names.
* Displayed the correct day based on the user's input.
* Added a default case to handle invalid inputs.
* Practiced decision-making and control flow concepts.
* Improved understanding of conditional branching in C++.
* Tested different inputs to verify the program's correctness.
This project helped me understand switch-case statements, user input handling, conditional logic, and basic program flow control in C++.
